Round 9 (2026-02-26)

What changed this round (landed)
- Landed code changes in:
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
- Two targeted AOT reductions:
  1) OP2 strict forcing upgraded from DP-only to full strict helper:
     - In head `OP2`, both strict operands now call `aot_force_strict(term, *s_pos)`
       (lhs always; rhs only in lhs==NUM branch).
     - This lets compiled OP2 WHNF-force `APP/ALO/REF` (plus bounded DP forcing)
       before deciding numeric fast-path vs residual OP2.
  2) Expression APP special-case for static REF fun:
     - `head=0` APP now recognizes `fun_tag == REF` and emits
       `term_new_app(heap_read(fun_loc), captured_arg)` directly.
     - This avoids whole-node `EXPR_APP_UNSUPPORTED_FUN` fallback for the common
       `@f(arg)` shape while preserving laziness of the argument via captured ALO.

Why
- Post-round-8 deopt hotspots were:
  - `EXPR_APP_UNSUPPORTED_FUN`
  - `EXPR_OP2_RHS_CAPTURE`
- On `gab_tak`/`gab_takl`, both came from the same strict OP2 frontier where lhs
  was an APP with REF head (`@len(_) + 1` pattern). The new APP(REF,...) emit path
  removes the unsupported-fun fallback there; stricter OP2 forcing resolves many
  APP/REF lhs terms to NUM and avoids RHS-capture fallback.

